WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.817 --> 00:00:03.877
- [Mark] Launa, Launa,

00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:06.016
Launa, where are you from originally?

00:00:06.016 --> 00:00:07.179
- Pennsylvania.

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:08.012
- [Mark] Pennsylvania,

00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:09.880
and how long have you been
down here in Skid Row?

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.040
- [Launa] About five years.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.577
- [Mark] Five years,

00:00:12.577 --> 00:00:14.890
and where do you stay, where do you sleep?

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:16.460
- [Launa] On Crocker.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.240
- [Mark] Do you have a tent?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.750
- I normally have a tent with my husband,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.200
however right now I don't.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.033
- [Mark] Where's your husband?

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:23.979
- He's in jail.

00:00:23.979 --> 00:00:25.710
- [Mark] He's in jail,
what is he in jail for?

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.042
- Possession.

00:00:27.042 --> 00:00:28.386
- [Mark] Possession.

00:00:28.386 --> 00:00:29.980
How much time do you get for possession?

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.020
- Normally you don't get that much time,

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.460
however I think that they may
be trying to go hard on him

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.320
because he's had a couple of cases before.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.610
So normally, you could
get out the same day

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.443
or a couple of days later,

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:47.183
but they're holding him 'til November.

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.110
- [Mark] What drug are
you using currently?

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:51.943
- [Launa] Heroin.

00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:54.220
- [Mark] Heroin, and
do you do meth as well?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.571
- [Launa] Oh, we mix it together.

00:00:55.571 --> 00:00:56.655
- [Mark] You mix it together,

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:57.488
do you smoke it?

00:00:57.488 --> 00:00:58.321
- [Launa] Shoot it.

00:00:58.321 --> 00:00:59.154
- [Mark] Shoot it, okay.

00:00:59.154 --> 00:01:00.960
What age did you start using drugs?

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.970
- [Launa] I didn't actually, well,

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.060
growing up, let's see,

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.870
around age 13 I smoked some weed,

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.700
from 13 to 20-something,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.633
then I quit using drugs all together.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:17.500
And then, I got real heavy
into cocaine for a while,

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.050
sniffing it,

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.020
quit, no problems,

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.950
then I got into crack,

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.980
and I did that for a good, a while,

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.016
and then I stopped doing the
crack and got into heroin,

00:01:30.016 --> 00:01:31.260
crystal meth.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.660
- [Mark] How much do you spend on,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:34.470
what does your addiction cost?

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.413
Heroin and meth, per week, let's say.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:39.740
- [Launa] I'd say probably

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.740
at least $100 and something a day.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.327
So you go $150 times
seven or $160 times seven.

00:01:48.327 --> 00:01:50.930
- [Mark] Yeah, so $150 a day.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.019
- [Launa] Yeah, $160.

00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:54.800
- [Mark] What do you guys do for money?

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.140
- Well, I get a VA pension,

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:02.140
and also my husband gets
social security, so.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.690
However, I quit drinking (laughs).

00:02:06.681 --> 00:02:07.520
- [Mark] It got you to stop drinking.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:11.950
- Yeah, I just chose
hard drugs instead, yay.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.181
- [Mark] And what's
going on with your arms?

00:02:13.181 --> 00:02:14.340
You've got bandages on both arms.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.750
- Yeah, these are from,

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:16.910
I'm not sure what they're from.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.770
They said that they were
from shooting heroin

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:19.700
and my arms got infected.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.130
They're doing a lot better,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:22.950
but I don't think that's the case.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:24.680
I don't know what the deal is,

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.750
they're really big holes.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.644
Yeah, they go pretty deep.

00:02:28.644 --> 00:02:30.912
- [Mark] How long have
you guys been married?

00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:33.083
- Well, we've been together since,

00:02:34.296 --> 00:02:37.730
well, we're not technically
married legally,

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.673
however I mean (indistinct) probably.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.830
- [Mark] And are you ever on the street

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.573
taking guys for money?

00:02:47.573 --> 00:02:48.457
- No.

00:02:48.457 --> 00:02:50.881
- [Mark] You don't do that?

00:02:50.881 --> 00:02:52.104
- No, I don't do that.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:55.590
- [Mark] And do you have children?

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.550
- I have children.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.420
- [Mark] Where are they?

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.260
- They're in Pennsylvania.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.560
- [Mark] Who's raising your kids?

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.140
- Their dad.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.140
I heard that my one son
got into a car crash,

00:03:07.875 --> 00:03:09.240
my oldest son,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.040
and ended up passing away.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.490
I don't know if that's true or not

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:15.590
because I haven't talked to them in years.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.080
I'm too afraid to call and find out.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:23.150
- [Mark] How old would be your kids?

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:27.900
- They would be, let's see,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.740
22 and

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:34.633
like 19,

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.373
22, 19.

00:03:36.373 --> 00:03:37.230
- [Mark] Boy or girl?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.262
- Two boys.

00:03:38.262 --> 00:03:39.410
- [Mark] Two boys.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.690
Tell me about your childhood.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.890
- My childhood was great.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.430
I'm an only child,

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.210
I don't have any brothers or sisters,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:48.080
mom, dad, grandma, aunt, uncle.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.223
My childhood was absolutely wonderful.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.780
I didn't go without,

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.680
I didn't get beat.

00:03:55.952 --> 00:03:56.897
- [Mark] Do you have both parents?

00:03:56.897 --> 00:03:58.441
- No, I didn't.

00:03:58.441 --> 00:04:01.150
I pretty much was raised by my grandma,

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.500
my mom worked all the time.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.370
But my childhood was wonderful.

00:04:08.391 --> 00:04:09.822
- [Mark] And no addiction,

00:04:09.822 --> 00:04:11.830
no alcoholism, anything like that?

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.935
- Well, my mom and my dad were alcoholics.

00:04:14.935 --> 00:04:15.768
- [Mark] They were?

00:04:15.768 --> 00:04:19.000
- However, they still maintained a job.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.320
We still had everything we needed,

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.710
got up and went to work everyday.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:25.080
I mean, yeah, they drank and
got messed up or whatever,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:28.370
they'd get, but, I mean,

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.690
my mom would wake up in the morning

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:31.449
and crack a beer as soon as she woke up.

00:04:31.449 --> 00:04:32.282
- [Mark] Oh, really.

00:04:32.282 --> 00:04:34.950
- Mm-hmm, but I'll tell you what,

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.440
she would drink all day and night,

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.490
the house would be clean,

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.850
we would have breakfast, lunch, dinner.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:42.377
You couldn't even really
tell if you asked me.

00:04:42.377 --> 00:04:44.760
- [Mark] And you were
drinking at one point?

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.160
- I didn't get into drinking
until I was in high school,

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.323
I started drinking.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.690
And that got kinda,

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.240
I got carried away with that,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:58.280
and I drank a whole lot, too much.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.750
- [Mark] And then you
transitioned to harder drugs.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.250
- Yeah, I quit for a while
and I didn't do anything,

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.630
I didn't do drugs or drink,

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.760
I was completely sober.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.480
I went on that, what
do you call, Antabuse.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.617
I was on Antabuse for three years.

00:05:11.617 --> 00:05:12.810
And so, for three years,

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.020
I didn't get high,

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.443
I didn't drink, nothing.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.870
I didn't like it,

00:05:22.339 --> 00:05:23.172
but I did it.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.260
It all went well,

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.530
and then I just decided
to start doing it again

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.523
because I was just,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.713
everything was just so dull.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:36.550
Really, it was,

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:39.480
I needed something to just change the pace

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:40.480
or do something different.

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.490
And I was bored and I
needed a new feeling,

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.900
I would wake up with the
same feeling everyday,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.670
same stuff everyday.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.094
And it just, fuck it,

00:05:48.094 --> 00:05:49.740
I'm just gonna start drinking again.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.573
So I did.

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:55.463
Then, when I came to California,

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:57.363
when I, yeah,

00:05:57.363 --> 00:06:00.210
when I went to California, wherever,

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:04.540
I went to go to school
to be a dog trainer,

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.640
certified dog trainer.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.090
I did that,

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:10.750
I didn't really go too far with that.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.390
I haven't done it yet, actually,

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:15.090
I didn't finish the school
because I injured my back,

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.400
and that's how I met my husband.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.950
And my husband had invited me over

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:23.163
to have a few beers,

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.300
and I never left (laughs).

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.483
We've been together ever since, so.

00:06:30.406 --> 00:06:31.920
- [Mark] Do you ever talk to your family?

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:33.170
- I don't have any family,

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.441
they're all dead.

00:06:34.441 --> 00:06:35.550
- [Mark] Your parents are gone?

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.730
- Yeah, my mom, my dad,

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.950
my gran, my aunts, my uncles.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.563
- [Mark] Just you and your sons?

00:06:41.407 --> 00:06:44.740
- And I think one of my
children are deceased.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.953
I think, I'm not sure.

00:06:47.402 --> 00:06:50.550
- [Mark] You don't feel
like reaching out to them?

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.700
- I'm kind of frightened to do so

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.110
because I mean,

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.603
I first of all,

00:06:59.837 --> 00:07:00.814
how difficult would that be?

00:07:00.814 --> 00:07:03.510
My first-born child passed away,

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:04.530
I knew nothing of it,

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:07.340
I was out doing drugs, drinking, partying,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:09.620
and I never even knew anything about it.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.063
Yeah, I'm not ready to
handle that yet, no.

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:18.160
So I haven't called to find out.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.310
I apologize, I mean, I know
that's an awful thing to say,

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.493
but I'm not ready to,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.920
there's nothing I could say.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:34.250
So I can't,

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.683
I mean, I could,

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.613
but I haven't.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.810
And I don't know if I will.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.229
- [Mark] In the next five years,
where would you like to be?

00:07:46.229 --> 00:07:47.594
Do you have any plans?

00:07:47.594 --> 00:07:51.194
- I don't know.

00:07:51.194 --> 00:07:52.980
I don't know.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.191
And then my other son,

00:07:55.191 --> 00:07:56.720
even if I did reach out to him,

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:57.720
what am I gonna say?

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:00.213
Hey, how you doing?

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:01.046
I fucked up,

00:08:01.046 --> 00:08:01.879
I'm still fucking up,

00:08:01.879 --> 00:08:02.980
I'm on the streets.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:05.210
I can't, I can't do that.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.800
I mean, I could, but I don't think,

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:13.370
that's not, this isn't
what I want them to see me.

00:08:14.960 --> 00:08:17.240
No, last time they saw me,

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.580
I went into the military,

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.263
I was strong,

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:22.003
and now look.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.313
I can't, I can't do that.

